{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>For a father of a multitude of nations.</b> A notarikon of his name. The resh that was in it at first — when he was a father only to Aram, which is his place — but now a father to all the world. It did not move from its place, for even the yod of Sarai cried out against the Shekhinah until it was added to Yehoshua, as it says: ״וַיִּקְרָא מֹשֶׁה לְהוֹשֵׁעַ בִּן נוּן יְהוֹשֻׁעַ״ (Numbers 13)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {0 "Rashi's wordplay assumes אברם = אב ארם, 'father of Aram'; the resh remains in אברהם though its referent shifts."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:59:01.974528020Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}